```     

### API Usage
```C#
        	Meter meter = new Meter("RecordingMeasurementsWithTagsList");
        	Counter<int> counter = meter.CreateCounter<int>("Counter");

            counter.Add(10, new TagList
                            {
                                { "Some Key", "Some Value" },
                                { "Some Other Key", 42 }
                            });

```     

### Old API Usage

```C#
    Meter meter = new Meter("MeterName");
    Counter<int> counter = meter.CreateCounter<int>("Counter");
    counter.Add(10, 
                new KeyValuePair<string, object?>("K1", "V1"),
                new KeyValuePair<string, object?>("K2", "V2"),
                new KeyValuePair<string, object?>("K3", "V3"),
                new KeyValuePair<string, object?>("K4", "V4"),
                new KeyValuePair<string, object?>("K5", "V5"),
                new KeyValuePair<string, object?>("K6", "V6"),
                new KeyValuePair<string, object?>("K7", "V7"),
                new KeyValuePair<string, object?>("K8", "V8");
```     


### Risks

It is low risk because all Metrics APIs as newly exposed and we are adding here overloads addressing the feedback we got on the original exposed APIs.

