cc @dotnet/fxdc 

* I assume the `GetEnumerator()` returns `Enumerator` and the interface returning one would be implemented explicitly.
* `TagsList.IsReadOnly` would always return `false`, so it should be implemented explicitly.
* The name `TagsList` feels add. I'd go with `TagList`.
* We need to make sure that default instances don't null reference, i.e. this code must work:
   ```C#
   new TagList
   {
        { "Some Key", "Some Value" },
        { "Some Other Key", 42 }
   }
   ```

